From ba01212eab874524cb7f4d6789f6c9a2fb723824 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Un1box <un1box@localhost>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:22:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] gles: resolve a presented frame's guest pages once

The synchronous present wrote a frame's rows into the guest one gles_guest_rw
at a time: 640 calls for a 960x640 frame, each probing its page, looking up the
current mmu index and splitting at the page boundary, to write 2.4 MB through
pointers that are the same for every row. Nothing runs in the guest while a
present copies, so the mapping cannot change under it.

Resolve the block once and copy the rows through it, on both the IOSurface path
and the readback path. A page that needs the full path -- a fault to be raised,
MMIO, dirty tracking -- fails the map, and the rows go back through
gles_guest_rw, which is also what raises the fault that reissues the present.
The GL thread's hook and a pending fault also choose that path, so the
behaviour of a page that is not there yet is unchanged.
